From a688ce2fc4d8cde9c5bf3544800c22e81e2ffd29 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand-build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:39:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: built for Android libc: video decoded by Android's
 hardware decoders

Chromium's Linux GPU process decodes only with VA-API and V4L2, which Android has not got, so on
Android's libc its media client is one of Spatiand's: MediaCodec, through the NDK, in the GPU
process, for the codecs this machine has a hardware decoder for (Android's software ones left to
Chromium's own), eight bits a sample. Each picture is copied into a frame of memory, which goes to
the page as shared memory. The renderer asks the GPU process for video decoders here as it does
with VA-API ("video_decoder" in mojo_media_services, AcceleratedVideoDecoder on by default).
---
